# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accepted security findings for aws-platform-infra.
# Every entry needs: WHY it is accepted + an expiry date for re-review.
# Changes to this file are reviewed in PRs like any other code.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# EKS public endpoint: no VPN/bastion in this project. Access is IAM-authenticated
# AND restricted to the Jenkins EIP + admin IP (public_access_cidrs). Prod: private endpoint + VPN.
AWS-0040 

# EKS secrets envelope encryption with a customer KMS key: skipped because dev is
# rebuilt nightly (KMS key churn/cost). Default AWS encryption applies. Prod: enable.
AWS-0039 

# Jenkins security group egress 0.0.0.0/0: needed to reach package repos, GitHub,
# Docker Hub and AWS APIs. Outbound only; inbound is restricted to admin + GitHub IPs.
AWS-0104 

# State bucket uses the AWS-managed KMS key (still KMS-encrypted, versioned, private).
# A customer-managed key adds cost without meaningful benefit for this project.
AWS-0132 